2. **`C_int γ^ρ`** — the bound on the nonlinear fluctuation part, with a
   source-derived exponent `ρ > 0`; the consumer side is
   `A1_margin_lower_bound`.
3. **`C_R`, `θ`** — the literal history-response kernel `R_{j,k} = ∂β_j/∂g_k` of
   the renormalisation-group map.  What such a bound buys, and how it follows
   from an irrelevant scaling dimension, is proved
   (`responseDecay_of_irrelevance`, `historyResponse_bound`); the kernel itself
   is not computed.

